A||||24||chester||Fiero 4 seater in New England||||14||
Z||000000||chester||08-27-2001||05:53 AM||||This is just a FYI to everyone that the 4 seater fiero is finally home in New England.  We started the journey Saturday morning at 10:00am and have just rolled in.  2450 miles on the odometer! This was a none stop drive from New Hampshire to Milwalkee Wisconson, load up and drive back.  I want to thank all involed EXPECIALLY Boomtastic and MsBeth for making the journey with us.  We couldn't have done it without you two!  I will post more about this including pics of the trip later today.  The keys are getting hard to deferentiate from lack of sleep.  So stay tuned!  Oh, and the pictures that were posted really don't do the car any justice.  Its SWEET!  Thanks John!<P>Rob D.<P>PS spell check don't seem to be working so please excuse any errors!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||14
Z||000001||FIERO JOHN-WI||08-27-2001||11:23 AM||||Robert, it was great to finally meet all 4 of you in person and realize you are just as fanatical as us in Wisconsin! I must admit I was sad when I saw you pull away. I have had a lot of time with that car, heck you already new that just by all the stuff I gave you about the car. My dad looked at me and said "Do you think Robert will finish it" I turned to him (as you were pulling away) and said Oh yeah he had that same look in his eyes as I did when I got it home from the frame shop. He said "what look is that" I said "that look that I have big plans for this car" Well I got to get back to work, I'm glad all of you made it home safe and sound. You know, now that it's home you will probably have to give tours of it (if you haven't allready) Enjoy and I'm lookingh forward to seeing some of those picks posted.  Later Fiero John||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||08-27-2001||11:38 AM||||Wow, Glad to hear you got it home safely  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> When are you inviting us up to look at it in person???  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Also we want pics.  Are you guys going to Marshfield Sunday, I hope to see you there.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000003||Elvira||08-27-2001||09:07 PM||||All I can say is "WOW, getting too old for this s**t!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"><BR>That was a looonngg trip, but well worth it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Elvira<BR>Blue 87GT<BR>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||11
Z||000004||chester||08-27-2001||09:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FIERO JOHN-WI:<BR><B>Robert, it was great to finally meet all 4 of you in person and realize you are just as fanatical as us in Wisconsin! I must admit I was sad when I saw you pull away. I have had a lot of time with that car, heck you already new that just by all the stuff I gave you about the car. My dad looked at me and said "Do you think Robert will finish it" I turned to him (as you were pulling away) and said Oh yeah he had that same look in his eyes as I did when I got it home from the frame shop. He said "what look is that" I said "that look that I have big plans for this car" Well I got to get back to work, I'm glad all of you made it home safe and sound. You know, now that it's home you will probably have to give tours of it (if you haven't allready) Enjoy and I'm lookingh forward to seeing some of those picks posted.  Later Fiero John</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Same here.  It was a pleasure!  If you’re ever in New England feel free to give me a jingle and you can come by and visit her.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The trip back was LONG! It was cool to see all the people on the highway do a double take when they saw the car.  We had people coming up to us at gas stations going "Never seen a stretch Fiero before!" We hit New York State and ran into the storm from hell. It poured thru the whole state. I was glad to get home.  2450 miles in 43 hours!  That’s the most insane trip for me yet!  Anyway thanks for everything and I'll keep you posted as to the progress of the project.  You never know, you might see it at the Dell's someday  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> .<P>Rob D. <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||6
Z||000005||Fiero5||08-27-2001||09:42 PM||||We are so excited in anticipation of seeing this Fiero! I agree, pics please. But more importantly, when can we come by for a cookout and check it out????<P>Also, since Sept 3rd is Marian and I's anniversary, we were thinking on seeing how many Fiero nuts would like to join us after the Spindles show for dinner??<P>Steve & Marian Kelley<P>------------------<BR>                                      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Glowing_Fiero9_sig.jpg">          <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
Z||000006||chester||08-27-2001||09:46 PM||||Here are some pics from the trip.<P>The Rig.  We used a Oldsmobile Bravada AWD loaded and a 18' car carrier for the trip.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trip_1.JPG"> <P><BR>The crew;<P><BR>MsBeth<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trip_3.JPG"> <P>Elvira ducking the camera<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trip_4.JPG"> <P>Boomtastic<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trip_6.JPG"> <P>And me<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trip_5.JPG"> <P>||||reg||7
